abstract: >-
  Honey steganography embeds a message in language-model output so that it is
  undetectable to a passive warden relative to a deployed cover sampler, and
  message-recovery-deniable under a matching plaintext model: every key yields a
  DTE draw (true message under the true key; independent decoy under a wrong
  key). Public key-independent segmentation closes a parse-count oracle; after
  public extraction the honey layer is classical DTE-then-OTP. Includes proofs
  and a GPT-2 reference implementation.
